From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] frd: Nintendo Network login against a server USCL runs
 (USCL_NEX)

Nintendo's NASC/NEX servers are gone, so a game's online mode stopped at
"Connecting to the Internet..." in frd:u RequestGameAuthentication (0x28),
which Azahar did not implement. Answer the NASC LOGIN locally:
- RequestGameAuthentication / GetGameAuthenticationData: USCL_NEX=<host>:<port>
  becomes the game server address (token USCL_NEX_TOKEN, default "uscl");
  without USCL_NEX the answer is NASC 110 "server no longer available";
- GetMyPassword: USCL_NEX_PASSWORD, the NEX (Kerberos) password;
- USCL_NEX_PID sets the principal id in GetMyFriendKey (Azahar leaves it 0);
- AttachToEventNotification, SetNotificationMask, Logout: simple stubs.
Layouts from libctru (frd.h GameAuthenticationData, 0x138 bytes).

Mario Kart 7 then asks for game server 0x00030600 and sends PRUDP v0 SYNs
to USCL_NEX (tested 2026-11-14; no NEX server answering yet).
